<internal_thoughts>
The robes. She's still wearing his robes. Forty years and she hasn't taken them off and I cannot look at them without seeing him in the doorway of my office the night before, telling me the containment matrix was unstable, and I told him the calculations were sound. The calculations were not sound. I knew within an hour. I have known for forty years. She wears his robes and she looks at me with trust she inherited from a man I killed through arrogance, and I fund her laboratory and I approve her requests and I will continue to do so until one of us is dead, and it will never be enough.
