"The texts are contradictory, which means one of two things: the scribes were mistaken, or the gods are. I find the second possibility far more interesting."
"Tantrus would have understood this. He would have looked at these readings and seen what I see — that the boundary is not a wall, it is a membrane, and something on the other side is aware that we are pressing against it. He would have told me to stop. He would have been right. I am not going to stop."
